// `root`, the family a package body accepts, is ambient: it is declared in the
// builtin package, so a file names it without importing anything.
//
// It describes every package rather than widgets, and while it lived in the ui
// package anything that wanted to be written at a file's root had to import
// the widget library to say so -- `output` could not, since the builtin
// package cannot import the ui one, and was let off the family check instead.
// Here a root member is declared in a file that imports nothing.
//
// It is not instantiated: a package-body node that is neither a window nor a
// directive is rendered by nothing today, and collecting one is the plugin
// plan's Phase 0 rather than this fixture's business.
//
// The package names are spelled out rather than as their URIs because the
// fuzz harness adds the standard imports to any source that mentions none.

component meta() root {}
